# CITATION.cff -- GitHub reads this and puts a "Cite this repository" button
# on the repository page. Format reference: https://citation-file-format.github.io
#
# THREE THINGS TO FILL IN BEFORE COMMITTING, all marked TODO below:
#   1. ORCID iDs, if you want them shown (optional, but they disambiguate you
#      from every other J. Keith in the literature).
#   2. date-released, which should match the date you publish the v0.3.1 tag.
#   3. The primer's year, publisher DOI and ISBN, once ACS assigns them.
#
# Once the primer is published, uncomment the preferred-citation block at the
# bottom. That tells citation managers "cite the book, not the code", which is
# usually what you want for a companion package.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
title: "gvbpp: GVB Perfect Pairing for PySCF"
type: software
version: 0.3.1
date-released: 2026-08-16   # TODO: match the date of the v0.3.1 release tag
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/keithgroup/gvbpp"
url: "https://github.com/keithgroup/gvbpp"

authors:
  - family-names: Keith
    given-names: "John A."
    email: jakeith@pitt.edu
    affiliation: "Department of Chemical and Petroleum Engineering, University of Pittsburgh"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # TODO

abstract: >-
  A standalone Generalized Valence Bond Perfect Pairing (GVB-PP) solver that
  runs entirely within PySCF. Each electron pair is correlated with a bonding
  and a correlating natural orbital, so bonds dissociate correctly without the
  combinatorial cost of a full CASSCF. Every pair carries a Coulson-Fischer
  overlap that behaves like a continuous bond order, which is what makes the
  method interpretive as well as numerical. Companion code for the ACS In Focus
  primer on the GVB description of chemical bonding.

keywords:
  - quantum chemistry
  - electronic structure
  - generalized valence bond
  - perfect pairing
  - valence bond theory
  - chemical bonding
  - PySCF

references:
  # The theory the package implements.
  - type: generic
    title: >-
      The Self-Consistent Field Equations for Generalized Valence Bond and
      Open-Shell Hartree-Fock Wave Functions
    authors:
      - family-names: Bobrowicz
        given-names: "Frank W."
      - family-names: Goddard
        given-names: "William A."
        name-suffix: III
    collection-title: "Methods of Electronic Structure Theory"
    editors:
      - family-names: Schaefer
        given-names: "Henry F."
        name-suffix: III
    publisher:
      name: "Plenum Press"
      city: "New York"
    year: 1977
    start: 79
    end: 127

  # The book this package accompanies.
  - type: book
    title: "The GVB Description of Chemical Bonding"
    authors:
      - family-names: Keith
        given-names: "John A."
        affiliation: "University of Pittsburgh"
      - family-names: Carter
        given-names: "Emily A."
        affiliation: "Princeton University"
      - family-names: Goddard
        given-names: "William A."
        name-suffix: III
        affiliation: "California Institute of Technology"
    collection-title: "ACS In Focus"
    publisher:
      name: "American Chemical Society"
      city: "Washington, DC"
    year: 2026        # TODO: confirm with ACS
    # doi: "10.1021/acsinfocus.XXXXXXX"   # TODO: add once assigned
    # isbn: "978-0-8412-XXXX-X"           # TODO: add once assigned

